<Defs>

  <!--
    The learned society (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release C"; DESIGN.md "Rimfolk's peoples"; Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/):
    scholars, copyists and booksellers who keep an archive of everything written down in the region and trade in books
    and knowledge. Industrial, on the game's outlander parent: a coat or gown dyed claret over a collar shirt, proctors in one kit
    of flak and the claret jacket to guard the archive (their kinds, below). Few towns (settlementGenerationWeight 0.45), each an archive with its reading hall
    and stacks (TownPlanDef Rimfolk_Plan_Archive); a bookseller's caravan of books, schematics and techprints (Royalty),
    no more often than another people's. A copyist of theirs asks to copy the colony's records for the archive
    (Rimfolk_Evt_ScholarCopyist); a travelling scholar, a book swapper, the old vault opened and the comet come from them
    likeliest (Patches/Rimfolk_PeoplesC.xml); once a year a fellow holds the night of the fire's disputation at the colony's
    gathering place (Rimfolk_Evt_Disputation). Their founding (the description): Ilse Varro, who carried eleven books
    and a ledger out of the burning archive at Hesk and copied them for the rest of her life. What they honour, fear and
    say is in their template (on their card). They defend their archives and raid only when the colony has turned them
    hostile (raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve 0.2). Listed once among the world's peoples when a world is made, never
    required. Faith (Ideology): a fixed creed of the self and of inquiry (Alpha Memes' monastic life where loaded, VE Memes'
    agnosticism among the structures it may take), the Islamic style's arched halls. Kind of people (Biotech): three in four baseliners; genies above all,
    highmates, high elves, the Avaloi, Alpha Genes' forsaken and Vanilla Races Expanded's archons.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Scholars</defName>
    <label>learned society</label>
    <description>A society of scholars, copyists and booksellers who keep an archive of everything written down in the region: histories, ledgers, letters, plans of machines and lists of the stars. They buy books, sell copies, and send their copyists to any town that keeps records of its own.\n\nTheir ways began the night the old archive at Hesk burned. A clerk named Ilse Varro carried out what she could in a handcart, eleven books and a ledger, and spent the rest of her life copying them for any town that would trade her a meal for a copy; the society is the people who learned to read from her pages. Every year on the night of the fire the fellows argue until dawn about what the archive held that nobody saved, and a scholar's first oath is to copy one thing that would otherwise be lost.\n\nThey are precise, digressive and fond of the word "strictly," and they never leave a question unasked. They would rather argue than fight, but their proctors keep rifles for the archive's sake. Each archive is kept by its archivist, and the society by its provost.</description>
    <pawnSingular>scholar</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>scholars</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>provost</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Scholars_Fellow</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Scholars</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_ScholarsTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/Scholars</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/ScholarsTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.48, 0.12, 0.26)</li>
      <li>(0.64, 0.24, 0.40)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <startingCountAtWorldCreation>1</startingCountAtWorldCreation>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <configurationListOrderPriority>16</configurationListOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.45</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve Inherit="False">
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.2)</li>
      </points>
    </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
    <xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
      <xenotypeChances>
        <Genie MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.1</Genie>
        <Highmate MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.03</Highmate>
        <DevDesigner_XenotypeHighElves MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,DevDesigner.Elves.Continued">0.04</DevDesigner_XenotypeHighElves>
        <DV_Avaloi MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,det.avaloi">0.03</DV_Avaloi>
        <AG_Forsaken MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,sarg.alphagenes">0.02</AG_Forsaken>
        <VRE_Archon MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Ludeon.RimWorld.Royalty,vanillaracesexpanded.archon">0.02</VRE_Archon>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Open Book</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>Nothing known should be lost. A scholar reads what was written, copies what is failing, and asks the question nobody else will; whatever can be written down is kept, and whatever is kept is lent. Each mind finds its own way to the truth, and the archive remembers all of them. What cannot be known is said so plainly, and argued over all the same, every year on the night of the fire.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Individualist</li>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphamemes">AM_Monastic</li>
    </forcedMemes>
    <structureMemeWeights Inherit="False">
      <Structure_Ideological MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">4</Structure_Ideological>
      <Structure_TheistAbstract MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">1</Structure_TheistAbstract>
      <!-- What cannot be known said plainly: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's agnosticism. -->
      <VME_Structure_Agnosticism MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">1</VME_Structure_Agnosticism>
    </structureMemeWeights>
    <styles>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Islamic</li>
    </styles>
    <caravanTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Caravan_Scholars</li>
    </caravanTraderKinds>
    <visitorTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Visitor_Scholars</li>
    </visitorTraderKinds>
    <baseTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Base_Scholars</li>
    </baseTraderKinds>
    <pawnGroupMakers Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <!-- A fight: the archive's proctors, a few fellows with pistols -->
        <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Proctor>10</Rimfolk_Scholars_Proctor>
          <Mercenary_Gunner>3</Mercenary_Gunner>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Fellow>2</Rimfolk_Scholars_Fellow>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Peaceful</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Fellow>20</Rimfolk_Scholars_Fellow>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Don>8</Rimfolk_Scholars_Don>
          <Villager_Child MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">4</Villager_Child>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Proctor>6</Rimfolk_Scholars_Proctor>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- A bookseller's caravan: crates of books on pack beasts, and proctors -->
        <kindDef>Trader</kindDef>
        <traders>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Bookseller>1</Rimfolk_Scholars_Bookseller>
        </traders>
        <carriers>
          <Muffalo>5</Muffalo>
          <Horse>4</Horse>
          <Dromedary>3</Dromedary>
          <Alpaca>2</Alpaca>
        </carriers>
        <guards>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Proctor>10</Rimfolk_Scholars_Proctor>
          <Mercenary_Gunner>2</Mercenary_Gunner>
        </guards>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Proctor>10</Rimfolk_Scholars_Proctor>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Fellow>8</Rimfolk_Scholars_Fellow>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Don>4</Rimfolk_Scholars_Don>
          <Rimfolk_Scholars_Bookseller>1</Rimfolk_Scholars_Bookseller>
        </options>
      </li>
    </pawnGroupMakers>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="ColonyCouncil.PeopleExtension">
        <calling>scholars</calling>
        <townWord>archive</townWord>
        <townWords>archives</townWords>
        <head>archivist</head>
        <heir>under-archivist</heir>
        <envoy>society fellow</envoy>
        <trader>bookseller</trader>
        <courier>copyist</courier>
        <couriers>copyists</couriers>
        <caravanWeight>1</caravanWeight>
        <camps>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_Scholars</li>
          <li>Council_Camp_Surveyors</li>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_Teacher</li>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_Watchers</li>
        </camps>
        <plan>Rimfolk_Plan_Archive</plan>
        <honours>the copied page, a good question and a patient reader</honours>
        <fears>fire, the lost book and the closed mind</fears>
        <sayings>
          <li>Nothing known should be lost.</li>
          <li>Copy it twice.</li>
          <li>Ask the question nobody will.</li>
          <li>Strictly speaking, that is two questions.</li>
        </sayings>
        <townGoods>
          <TextBook>3~6</TextBook>
          <Novel>2~4</Novel>
          <Schematic>1~3</Schematic>
          <Cloth>40~90</Cloth>
          <MedicineIndustrial>2~6</MedicineIndustrial>
          <Silver>100~250</Silver>
        </townGoods>
        <ariseAges>1~3</ariseAges>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </FactionDef>

  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md "Their gear, their kinds of people and their gifts"): scholars vary freely
    around their signature, an outer coat or academic gown dyed claret (a robe, a jacket, a duster, Vanilla Apparel
    Expanded's suit jackets and lab coats) over a collar shirt, the rest the game's industrial clothes and the mods'
    (Vanilla Apparel Expanded's scarves, berets, boots), the bookseller's bowler, the provost's beret (Royalty). The archive's proctors are its guards and wear one kit: a flak vest under the
    claret jacket, the game's guns and Vanilla Weapons Expanded - Non-Lethal's tasers, dart guns and stun batons. They
    carry books: textbooks, novels, schematics. A few are A RimWorld of Magic's arcanists, enchanters or chronomancers, and
    a few have a psylink (Royalty; with Vanilla Psycasts Expanded, a chronopath's or an empath's path). Without any mod:
    robes, jackets and dusters, the game's shirts, trousers and hats, a flak vest and its guns.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef Name="Rimfolk_ScholarsKindBase" Abstract="True">
    <race>Human</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>Rimfolk_Scholars</defaultFactionDef>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.04</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>0.02</backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>
    <invNutrition>2.55</invNutrition>
    <specificApparelRequirements>
      <!-- Claret on the proctors' jackets and the provost's cape, whoever wears one. -->
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_Jacket</apparelDef><color>(0.56, 0.18, 0.32)</color></li>
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_Cape</apparelDef><color>(0.56, 0.18, 0.32)</color></li>
    </specificApparelRequirements>
  </PawnKindDef>

